 data-sqsp-block=\"video\" data-website-component-id=\"yui_3_17_2_1_1589740545350_107407\" id=\"block-yui_3_17_2_1_1589740545350_107407\"><div class=\"sqs-block-content\">\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  <div class=\"intrinsic\" style=\"max-width:100%\">\n    \n      \n    \n    <div\n      class=\"embed-block-wrapper\"\n      style=\"padding-bottom:56.25%;\"\n    >\n      <div\n        class=\"sqs-video-wrapper\"\n        data-provider-name=\"\"\n        data-html=\"&lt;iframe src=&quot;//www.youtube.com/embed/Vlwnntpleac?wmode=opaque&amp;amp;enablejsapi=1&quot; height=&quot;270&quot; width=&quot;480&quot; scrolling=&quot;no&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;&quot;&gt;\n&lt;/iframe&gt;\"\n        data-localized=\"{&quot;invalidVideo&quot;:&quot;Invalid video embed.&quot;,&quot;playButton&quot;:&quot;Play&quot;}\"\n        data-config-loading=\"\"\n      >\n        \n          <div class=\"sqs-video-overlay\" style=\"opacity: 0\">\n            <img\n              data-load=\"false\"\n              data-mode=\"cover\"\n              data-src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/5da7d49f6a98d112691e4bbc/1589744740513-V1JGLNNBF70AXU0ZGX4T/IMG_8917.jpg\"\n              data-image-focal-point=\"0.5,0.5\"\n            />\n            <div class=\"sqs-video-opaque\"></div>\n            <div class=\"sqs-video-icon\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\" aria-label=\"Play\"></div>\n          </div>\n        \n      </div>\n    </div>\n    \n    \n\n\n\n  </div>\n\n\n<style class=\"transform-overrides-vars\">\n  \n</style>\n\n\n\n  \n  \n  \n<style id=\"container-styles\">#block-yui_3_17_2_1_1589740545350_107407 {\n    \n    \n    \n  }\n\n  #block-yui_3_17_2_1_1589740545350_107407 .intrinsic {\n    \n    }\n\n  #block-yui_3_17_2_1_1589740545350_107407 {\n      mix-blend-mode: var(--tweak-video-block-blend);\n      border-radius: var(--tweak-video-block-radius);\n  }\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n  \n</style>\n\n<style id=\"override-container-styles\">\n    @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n          \n            \n\n#block-yui_3_17_2_1_1589740545350_107407 {\n            \n            }\n        }\n    \n  \n    @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n          #block-yui_3_17_2_1_1589740545350_107407 .intrinsic {\n            \n            }\n        }\n    \n  @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n          \n          \n\n          \n          \n          \n        }</style>\n\n  <style>#block-yui_3_17_2_1_1589740545350_107407 { border-width: 0; height: auto; }</style>\n  \n  \n  \n    <style>\n    \n      \n    \n      \n        @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n          #block-yui_3_17_2_1_1589740545350_107407 { background-color: transparent; }\n          #block-yui_3_17_2_1_1589740545350_107407 .intrinsic { background-color: var(--tweak-video-block-background-color); }\n        }\n      \n    \n    </style>\n  \n\n</div></div><div class=\"sqs-block html-block sqs-block-html\" data-block-type=\"2\" data-sqsp-block=\"text\" id=\"block-yui_3_17_2_1_1589740545350_74775\"><div class=\"sqs-block-content\">\n\n<div class=\"sqs-html-content\" data-sqsp-text-block-content>\n  <p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Don’t be scared of hot Italian sausage. It gives the soup the right kick - without being overly spicy. I would argue regular sweet Italian sausage wouldn’t work as well, but if that’s all you have, go for it — but maybe throw in a pinch of red pepper flakes for good measure. </p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">You can also make this vegetarian and skip the meat entirely and sub veggie broth instead of chicken broth. <br><br>Give this recipe a try and let me know what you think! I am also posting the BEST sourdough bread recipe, which I highly recommend making as an accompaniment to this soup. Enjoy! </p><p class=\"\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\"></p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\"><strong>RECIPE | CREAMY, DREAMY TORTELLINI SOUP</strong></p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\"><strong>Ingredients:</strong></p><ul data-rte-list=\"default\"><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">3 links hot Italian sausage (casings removed)</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">2 carrots, diced</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">2 celery stalks, diced&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">1 small yellow onion, diced&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">2 tablespoons tomato paste&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">1/2 cup red wine</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">1/4 cup all purpose flour&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">1 bay leaf</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">20 oz. cheese tortellini (buy fresh pasta, from the refrigerated aisle)</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">2 cups baby spinach (loosely packed)</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">1.5 quarts chicken broth&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">1 cup half and half</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">3/4 cup grated Parmesan cheese, plus extra for serving</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">6-8 fresh basil leaves, torn (or about a teaspoon if using dried)</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">2 sprigs fresh oregano (or ½ teaspoon if using dried)</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Salt and pepper to taste&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\"><strong>Instructions:</strong></p><ol data-rte-list=\"default\"><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Crumble the sausage (using a little olive oil) in a sturdy soup pot. Cook through, breaking it all up with a spatula or wooden spoon.</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Add the celery, carrot, and onion and saute at medium-low until they soften (about 7-10 minutes), being careful not to brown them. Add salt.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Create a space in the middle of the pot and add the tomato paste. Stir into the vegetables.</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Add the red wine, and stir everything together. Cook for 1 minute.</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Add the flour and stir quickly, using a whisk. Add a little broth if it’s too dry and keep whisking until the flour is completely absorbed.</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Add the remaining broth + the oregano and bay leaf. Bring to a boil, stirring to ensure the roux (aka flour mixture) is evenly distributed throughout. Once it’s at a rolling boiling, bring down to a simmer (medium low).</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Simmer for ~15 minutes. You want the veggies to cook through and the broth will also thicken a bit.</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Add the tortellini, half and half, cheese, salt and pepper. Make sure there’s a light boil going. </p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Once tortellini are cooked through, add the spinach and fresh basil.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Serve with Parmesan cheese and a hunk of bread for mopping up the broth! </p></li></ol>\n</div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</div></div><div class=\"sqs-block image-block sqs-block-image\" data-block-type=\"5\" data-sqsp-block=\"image-classic\" id=\"block-yui_3_17_2_1_1589740545350_76013\"><div class=\"sqs-block-content\">\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    <div\n        class=\"\n          image-block-outer-wrapper\n          layout-caption-below\n          de